# Rule 00. Zones and vocabulary

Language-agnostic. The words below are used by rules 01, 02, 03 and 06 and by the
runtime appendices (`runtime-svelte.mdc`, `runtime-react.mdc`, `runtime-vue.mdc`).

## Zones

| Zone | What lives there | Rules 01 to 06 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kit (`{kit}`) | primitives and utils: the only place that knows host tags | Do not apply. Raw HTML, dynamic tags and computed ARIA are allowed. |
| Composition | blocks, composite components, app screens and templates | Apply. |
| Generated | any file with the `Code generated by xgen. DO NOT EDIT.` header | No hand edits (`xgen check` group `drift`). The rules still apply: fix the spec, the authoring builder or the emitter. |

`{kit}` is a placeholder for the kit dirs of the package at hand. In
`packages/<rt>/ui` it is `src/primitives` and `src/utils` (plus `src/styles`).

## Where the paths come from

Every package or app declares its own zones in the `ui8kit` field of its `package.json`:

```json
"ui8kit": { "runtime": "vue", "kit": ["src/primitives", "src/utils", "src/styles"], "composition": ["src/blocks", "src/components"], "blockRoot": ["src/blocks"] }
```

- `runtime`: `svelte`, `react` or `vue`.
- `kit`, `composition`: dirs or files relative to the package.
- `blockRoot`: the part of the composition whose files must open on `Block` (blocks and screens).
- `generated`: `true` when xgen writes the package (the field is then set in the generator, not by hand).

`bun packages/tooling/bin/zones.mjs --write` assembles the catalog `rules/zones.json`.
`bun run check` (group `rules`) fails when the catalog is stale. Anything outside
both zones (plain TypeScript, data, entry files) is not scanned by the composition rules.

Current catalog (see `rules/zones.json` for the source of truth):

| Package | Runtime | Kit | Composition | Block root |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `packages/{svelte,react,vue}/ui` | each | `src/primitives`, `src/utils`, `src/styles` | `src/blocks`, `src/components` | `src/blocks` |
| `apps/host-{svelte,react,vue}` | each | `xgen/runtime` | `xgen/screens` | `xgen/screens` |
| `apps/magazine` | svelte | `src/lib` | `src/App.svelte`, `src/parts`, `src/templates` | `src/App.svelte`, `src/templates` |
| `apps/discovery` | svelte | none | `src/App.svelte`, `src/parts` | `src/App.svelte` |
| `packages/taste-screens` | svelte | `src/recipes` | `src/screens`, `src/parts` | `src/screens` |
| `packages/panorama` | svelte | `src` | none | none |

## Vocabulary

| Term | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Raw HTML injection | Rendering an HTML string as markup instead of building nodes. |
| Dynamic tag | Choosing the host element at run time from a value. |
| Raw native tag | A lowercase HTML element name written in a composition template. |
| Reactive ARIA state | An `aria-*` attribute whose value is an expression of state or props. |
| Component root | The first rendered node of a component file, ignoring control flow wrappers. |
| Literal text | Visible or announced words written in the template or in a text prop instead of coming from content. |
| Two-way binding | A binding that writes back into the parent state. |

The per-runtime syntax of each term is in the runtime appendix of that stack.

## The gate

`bun run check` runs the group `rules` of `xgen check`: per-runtime adapters
parse every composition file into one small tree, and shared detectors report
`block-root`, `raw-html`, `dynamic-tag`, `raw-native-tag`, `reactive-aria` and
`literal-text`. The kit zone is never scanned. Existing violations are recorded
per package in `rules/baselines/<package>.json`; a new one fails the check.
